<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="033" project="field-mapping-server-write-path-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>System creators (To Do generation, TaskActionCore, SignalWriter, DecisionRecordWriter) create through the system principal (FR-21 part a)</title>
    <phase>3 W3 Product creators onto the service</phase>
    <gate>019 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .cs in Sprk.Bff.Api; tags include bff-api, jobs, ai-nodes, ownership; touches ontology-owned writers with a restricted writer identity (security); adds tests at KEEP paths (TEST-MODIFYING override).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Four creators with different identities, owner contexts and existing documented exceptions; the system principal skips as-caller checks, so each conversion needs judgment about what authorization is already established upstream.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>W3-server</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>019</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, jobs, ai-nodes, ownership, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>10-14 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Route four system creators through `RecordCreationService` using the SYSTEM principal (`RequestedBy` when known): To Do generation (`Services/Workspace/TodoGenerationService.cs` create ~:1082), playbook create-task (`Services/Ai/Nodes/ActionCore/TaskActionCore.cs` create ~:315), `Services/Signals/SignalWriter.cs` (create ~:583) and `Services/Signals/DecisionRecordWriter.cs` (create ~:1223). Existing accepted ownership exceptions become NAMED registry rules with a rationale. Do NOT decide the `DecisionRecordWriter` communication-owner case (~:1479); record it for task 060.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, .NET 10 BFF, background/AI-node writers and the ontology Signal/Decision write path. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>Each of the four creators makes its row create through the service with the system principal and gets the same owner, stamp and mapping a caller create under the same parent would get; every existing exception is a named registry rule; the census test lists each creator as routed.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-21 (part a), FR-07 (system principal skips the as-caller checks, steps 2 and 5, and applies every other step identically), FR-11 (registry exceptions). Today: `TodoGenerationService` resolves the owner itself (`ResolveOwnerAsync` over the parents, `RecordOwnerUnresolvedException`) and calls `_dataverse.CreateAsync` (~:1082); `TaskActionCore.CreateAsync` (~:155) resolves the owner (~:285-300), applies Assigned To defaults and calls `_entityService.CreateAsync` (~:315); `SignalWriter` builds the entity and calls `_writerClient.CreateAsync` (~:583); `DecisionRecordWriter` calls its private `CreateAsync` (~:1205) over `_writerClient.CreateAsync` (~:1223) and documents that the ONLY identity holding Create on the Decision Record table is the ontology writer identity (no human role, no Write or Delete). That writer identity is a deliberate least-privilege design owned by ontology-r1; whether the unified service can create under it is an open point (see escalation). Existing exceptions to preserve: unfiled communications keep the creator (`UnfiledOwnership.KeepCreator`), direct threads, notifications, and the Decision Record's D-144/D-169 communication-owner principal (not decided here).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Workspace/TodoGenerationService.cs (owner ~:1050-1075; create ~:1082)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Nodes/ActionCore/TaskActionCore.cs (CreateAsync ~:155; owner ~:285; create ~:315)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalWriter.cs (BuildEntity / owner ~:540-583; create ~:583)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecisionRecordWriter.cs (owner resolution ~:1440-1480; CreateAsync ~:1205-1223)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordTableRules.cs (named exception rules with rationale)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests.cs (list each of the four as routed; UAC-r2 also edits census tests, run /conflict-check)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/OntologyWriterDataverseClient.cs (the writer identity)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/RecordCreation/RecordCreationService.cs (system principal, tasks 013-016)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/seam/Signals/SignalWriterSeamTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/seam/Signals/DecisionRecordWriterSeamTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/seam/Communication/CreateTaskApplySeamTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/OntologyWriterAppendToGuardTests.cs (must keep passing)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/data-mutation/Signals/SystemCreatorsThroughServiceTests.cs (each creator uses the system principal and gets caller-equivalent owner, stamp and mapping)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="019" status="required">W2 service deployed and reviewed.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-008 (path A, spec ADR Tensions)">Scope: authorization. These are non-HTTP callers, which is exactly why payload-dependent checks live in `CallerWriteAuthorization` and not in filters. The system principal skips only the as-caller checks; authorization already established upstream (the job's scope, the playbook run's user, the review's decider) stays where it is. Add no inline authorization to the writers.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Scope: refusals. Writers keep their existing failure types (`RecordOwnerUnresolvedException`, `DecisionRecordRefusedException`, `OntologyWriterFailureReason.OwnerRefused`, TaskActionCore's `Guid.Empty` return); a service refusal maps to them; no raw upstream text in any returned value.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: identity. System principal = app-only under the managed identity, `RequestedBy` recorded when the originating user is known (playbook run user, review decider). The system principal must never be reachable from an HTTP caller-controlled flag. The Signal and Decision writers' restricted writer identity must not gain wider privileges.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-010">Scope: DI. Writers obtain the scoped service per job/message scope as they already obtain other scoped services (TodoGenerationService and SignalWriter already create scopes); no new registration; no static service locator.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-052 / ADR-036">Scope: jobs. Job handlers keep their idempotency and lease semantics; a redelivered job must not create a duplicate row; the service create is not retried blindly after an ambiguous failure (NFR-03).</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-01 (spec)">Scope: all four creators. Fail closed: an unresolved owner refuses and writes nothing (today TodoGenerationService throws, TaskActionCore returns Guid.Empty, writers refuse); never fall back to an app-owned row. The only non-team owners are the registry-named exceptions.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-08 / CLAUDE.md §8.5">Scope: coordination. ontology-r1 owns SignalWriter, DecisionRecordWriter and the decision cores; UAC-r2 PR #2110 also edits census tests. Run /conflict-check FIRST; sequence with the owning projects; do not rewrite writer internals beyond the create and owner call sites.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: communication-owner case. The `DecisionRecordWriter` communication-owner principal (D-144/D-169, ~:1479) is preserved exactly as today and recorded in the task notes as an open assessment item for task 060. Do not decide whether it is an exception or must change.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: BFF publish. Placement Justification in the PR; fresh-master publish-size delta per §10.4; `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive`; no package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests added or modified. KEEP paths; no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;; no DI-registration tests. Existing seam and guard tests change only to follow a moved dependency, never by weakening an assertion. Cover the stated contract plus the named edge cases only.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>System principal creates; ontology writers; ownership exceptions</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-002-thin-plugins.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-008-endpoint-filters.md</file>
