    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="entity-operations" location=".claude/patterns/dataverse/entity-operations.md">Create payload shapes.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor; read spec FR-21 and FR-07; read the four create sites and their owner contexts; re-grep each creator's existing tests.</step>
    <step order="1">Run /conflict-check (ontology-r1, UAC-r2 PR #2110 census tests). Record the result and sequencing. Escalate if a PR rewrites the writers' create methods.</step>
    <step order="2">Inventory, in the task notes, each creator's current exception behaviour (owner context, KeepCreator, assignee rules, Assigned To defaults) and the registry rule that will carry it, with rationale.</step>
    <step order="3">Write failing tests first: for each creator, a system create under a Matter yields the same owner, I-1 stamp and mapping (if profiled) as a caller create under the same Matter (FR-07 acceptance); an unresolved owner writes nothing; a redelivered job creates no duplicate; census lists each as routed.</step>
    <step order="4">Convert To Do generation and TaskActionCore (plain app-only creators): pass the originating user as `RequestedBy`; delete their private owner resolution and creator stamping where the service supplies it; keep AssignedToDefaults semantics via the registry "for"-person rule.</step>
    <step order="5">Convert SignalWriter and DecisionRecordWriter only at their create and owner call sites; keep the restricted writer identity question open if the service cannot use it (escalation). Preserve D-123 secure-if-any, D-134 personal To Do assignee and the communication-owner principal exactly.</step>
    <step order="6">Add the named exception rules to the registry; extend RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests so each of the four is listed as routed (add a negative control only if the census harness already supports them; otherwise leave negative controls to task 061).</step>
    <step order="7">Build; run Signals seam tests, CreateTaskApplySeamTests, TodoGeneration tests, OntologyWriterAppendToGuardTests, SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests*, DecisionCommit tests, RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests; publish-size delta; CVE check.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="9">Document any deviation in projects/field-mapping-server-write-path-r1/notes/ (including the communication-owner item for task 060).</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the unified service cannot create the Signal or Decision Record under the restricted ontology writer identity without granting the managed identity Create on those tables or widening the writer identity, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 (security-sensitive: auth/identity) and §6.5 with options; do not change role privileges.</trigger>
    <trigger>DecisionRecordWriter communication-owner case: do not decide. Preserve current behaviour, record the finding for task 060, and continue.</trigger>
    <trigger>If /conflict-check shows ontology-r1 or UAC-r2 is rewriting any of the four create methods, STOP and ask the human to sequence the work.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Grep `_dataverse!.CreateAsync` (TodoGenerationService.cs ~:1082), `_entityService.CreateAsync` (TaskActionCore.cs ~:315), `_writerClient.CreateAsync` (SignalWriter.cs ~:583, DecisionRecordWriter.cs ~:1223): four private create paths, each with its own owner resolution. Existing tests: tests/integration/seam/Signals/SignalWriterSeamTests.cs and DecisionRecordWriterSeamTests.cs, tests/integration/seam/Communication/CreateTaskApplySeamTests.cs; none compares system-principal and caller-principal results under one parent.</existing>
    <extension>Yes for production code: callers convert to the existing service, no new production file (exceptions are registry rows). The only new file is a test class, because the existing writer seam suites must pass unchanged and none asserts caller/system equivalence (FR-07 acceptance).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>System-created To Dos, tasks, Signals and Decision Records keep four private owner paths and skip field mapping and the standard stamp/search-index steps, so they drift from the standard and are invisible to the census guard (spec FR-21, section 11 table).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test .NET</tool>
    <tool name="skill:conflict-check">Detect overlap with ontology-r1 and UAC-r2</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
