    <output type="test">tests/integration/data-mutation/Signals/SystemCreatorsThroughServiceTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests.cs (four creators listed as routed)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">To Do generation, `TaskActionCore`, `SignalWriter` and `DecisionRecordWriter` each create through `RecordCreationService` with the system principal, and the census test lists each as routed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">For each creator, a system create under a Matter yields the same owner, I-1 stamp and (where a profile exists) mapping as a caller create under the same Matter.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each existing ownership exception (unfiled communications keep the creator, direct threads, notifications, and any exception these four creators relied on) is a NAMED registry rule with a written rationale.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The `DecisionRecordWriter` communication-owner principal (D-144/D-169) behaves exactly as before and the open assessment is recorded in the task notes for task 060.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an unresolved owner writes nothing for each creator and surfaces the creator's existing failure type (exception, `Guid.Empty`, or writer refusal); no app-owned fallback row is created.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a redelivered job or playbook run does not create a duplicate row, and the system principal is not reachable from any HTTP request field (asserted by a test or a grep recorded in the notes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF build 0 errors; Signals seam tests, CreateTaskApplySeamTests, OntologyWriterAppendToGuardTests, SecureChildOwnershipAiToolTests*, DecisionCommit tests and RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests pass; publish-size delta, CVE result and /conflict-check result recorded in the task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">From task 014 (decision 4) and task 016 (review pass 1 F1-d), 2026-10-21: add the APP-ONLY column-metadata reader (type, IsValidForCreate, IsValidForUpdate, MaxLength, date behaviour, money columns) for the system principal. Reuse the shape of the caller-side reader that `RecordCreationService.Mapping.cs` `MapFieldsAsync` uses; extending the existing app-only `MetadataService` is preferred over a new reader (root CLAUDE.md §11). Wire it into BOTH the system-principal create path (so a system principal with a mapping stops being an argument error) AND Repair (`RecordCreationService.Repair.cs`, which today writes mapped values unchecked: one bad rule fails the whole update every pass, K-1 in notes/task-016-notes.md). Repair drops a value whose column is unknown, not ValidForUpdate, the wrong type (`Fits`), over MaxLength, or of an unknown date behaviour, with a reason, and still writes the other fields. Tests: an int literal into a Decimal column, an unknown column, an over-length string.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Owner decision 2026-10-21 (Repair field security, option 1; UAC-r2 concurs). Using the app-only metadata reader above, Repair (`RecordCreationService.Repair.cs`, the `TODO(task 033)` seam) skips every source column that is field-secured (`IsSecured`), under UAC-r2's conditions:
      (1) fail closed: if the metadata read faults or a source column's IsSecured is unknown, map NOTHING for that row, with reason `record_repair.mapping_source_metadata_unavailable`; never fall back to "not secured"; read metadata per pass or cache briefly, so a column that becomes secured is honoured on the next pass;
      (2) the document access and D7 link columns stay refused through RefuseAppOnlyWrite (already in 016);
      (3) the #2188 guard keeps its per-occurrence allow-list entry for Repair's single ApplyFillOnly call (added in 016); update its reason if the wording changes;
      (4) tests: must-fire, a field-secured source column is not copied; must-fire, a metadata fault maps nothing; must-not-fire, an unsecured column is still filled.
      (5) Task 052 stays blocked until this criterion is met.
    </criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-21 part a, FR-07, FR-11, NFR-01, NFR-08. Inbound communication and document ingestion are task 034. The ownership matrix and exception assessment (notification outbox, Decision Record communication owner) are task 060.</notes>

